"{\n  \"reasoning\": \"GBW >=20MHz requires gm1 >= 2\u03c0\u00b720e6\u00b72pF \u2248 250\u00b5S. Choosing gm/Id = 10 gives Id (M1) = gm1/gmid = 25\u00b5A, so Itail = 2\u00b7Id = 50\u00b5A. Power = 3.3V\u00b72\u00b7Itail = 330\u00b5W < 400\u00b5W. With L1=0.5\u00b5m (NMOS) gm/gds\u2248174, giving gds2\u224825\u00b5A/174\u22480.144\u00b5S. Using L3=2\u00b5m (PMOS) gm/gds\u22481258, giving gds4\u224825\u00b5A/1258\u22480.020\u00b5S. Total gds\u22480.164\u00b5S, so A0\u2248gm1/gds\u2248250\u00b5S/0.164\u00b5S\u22481525 (\u224863dB) >40dB. Mirror pole is pushed high by the long L=2\u00b5m on M3, ensuring phase margin >60\u00b0. Slew rate = Itail/CL = 50\u00b5A/2pF = 25V/\u00b5s, and output swing >1.5V is satisfied with the chosen over\u2011drive voltages. All specs are met.\",\n  \"gmid1\": 10,\n  \"L1_um\": 0.5,\n  \"gmid3\": 10,\n  \"L3_um\": 2,\n  \"gmid5\": 10,\n  \"L5_um\": 2,\n  \"Itail_uA\": 50\n}"